From: Igor Sheludko <ishell@chromium.org>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 15:37:46 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] [Backport] CVE-2026-118320: Memory corruption in V8

Manual cherry-pick of patch originally reviewed on
https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/v8/v8/+/8576038:
Synchronize concurrent GetPrototypeTransition in TryUpdateNoLock

Make TransitionsAccessor::GetPrototypeTransition an instance method on
TransitionsAccessor and guard prototype transition cache lookups with
full_transition_array_access() when accessed concurrently from
MapUpdater::TryUpdateNoLock.

This pairs with the full_transition_array_access() lock already held in
TransitionsAccessor::PutPrototypeTransition during compaction and new
entry publication, preventing concurrent readers from observing
partially-initialized maps or in-progress array compactions.

Fixed: 568894515

TAG=agy
CONV=d848b9e2-cbea-4f48-a8e4-dec738f151e6

